# Audit report -- Phase 270: the gate mode is weaker than the mode it replaced

**Verdict**: PASS
**Target**: docs/plan-qor-phase270-post-anchor-weaker-than-verify.md (iteration 4)
**Session**: 2026-09-07T2035-2f4c25
**Issues**: GH #443, GH #425, GH #430
**Mode**: adversarial; independent architecture reviewer holding Read/Grep/Glob only, executing nothing
**Iterations**: 4 (1-3 VETO), plus four binding amendments applied before this report

## Scope

Covers that both modes walk one unresolvable-entry ladder; that the boundary is resolved by argument, then declaration, then auto-detection permitted only when a strict evaluation would raise nothing, then a fail-closed refusal; that a linkage break is disclosed only when both members of its pair sit at or below an asserted boundary; and that five fixtures encoding the old weakness are decided rather than discovered.

## Blocking grounds raised and cleared

1. The proposed linkage pass closed neither issue it claimed: continuity resets across an unresolvable entry, so it emitted nothing on the tainted-anchor fixture.
2. The same design rebuilt the detection window the brief diagnosed: one honest append after a fork moved the boundary past it.
3. The remedy named in the failure message reached only the CLI; three of four consumers had no parameter to forward.
4. Two design points contradicted each other on the same entry, proven on the fixture the plan cited as its own precedent.
5. The auto-detection gate admitted a forked ledger, because a fork produces no failing per-entry classification.
6. The central clause existed in the gate artifact and not in the plan the seal binds.
7. Four binding amendments: a heading asserting the removed rule, a stale reach claim, an untested pair rule, and a test that would have passed for an incidental reason.

## Limits

The reviewer executed nothing across six verdicts and has read none of the implementation. Every measurement is the author's and unwitnessed. It predicted, by fixture arithmetic, the five tests that would break; all five broke. An entry heading not matching the entry pattern is invisible to both modes and to any version of the gate: not introduced here, not fixable here, recorded so the next reader does not rediscover it.
